hertz (cycles per second).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="16349">audio</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="473281">ಆಡಿಯೋ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10452_107217_3042582"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In color management, the purity of a color's hue, moving from gray to the pure color.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="107217">saturation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3042582">ಶುದ್ಧತ್ವ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10459_116136_2177899"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of markup in markup languages. A start tag is the starting element of a tag pair which contains metainformation about some part of the text.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="116136">start tag</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2177899">ಆರಂಭಿಕ ಟ್ಯಾಗ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><