xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The suite of networking protocols arranged in four layers, which are called the link layer, internet layer, transport layer, and application layer, and that includes IP in the internet layer and TCP in the transport layer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="120227">TCP/IP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="473988">TCP/IP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1379_120227_473989"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The suite of networking protocols arranged in four layers, which are called the link layer, internet layer, transport layer, and application layer, and that includes IP in the internet layer and TCP in the transport layer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="120227">TCP/IP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="473989">ಪ್ರಸಾರ ನಿಯಂತ್ರಣ ಪ್ರೊಟೋಕಾಲ್/ಇಂಟರ್ನೆಟ್ ಪ್ರೊಟೋಕಾಲ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1379_120228_473988"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The suite of networking protocols arranged in four layers, which are called the link layer, internet layer, transport layer, and application layer, and that includes IP in the internet layer and TCP in the transport layer.</descrip></descripGrp>