r interface implemented by a software application via a component of a web server, such as IIS.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1054905">web portal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956936">ವೆಬ್ ಪೋರ್ಟಲ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22781_1054938_2290068"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To permit someone else to perform an action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1054938">allow</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2290068">ಅನುಮತಿಸು</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2279_26594_473351"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A piece of software that functions as an electronic calendar used for scheduling.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="26594">calendar program</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="473351">ಕ್ಯಾಲೆಂಡರ್ ಪ್ರೋಗ್ರಾಂ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2279_26594_474714"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A piece of software that functions as an electronic calendar used for scheduling.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="26594">calendar program</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="474714">ಕ್ಯಾಲೆಂಡರ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2279_294450_473351"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A piece of software that functions as an electronic calendar used for scheduling.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="294450">calendar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="473351">ಕ್ಯಾಲೆಂಡರ್ ಪ್ರೋಗ್ರಾಂ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2279_294450_474714"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A piece of software that functions as an electronic calendar used for scheduling.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="294450">calendar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="474714">ಕ್ಯಾಲೆಂಡರ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22823_1055132_1251284"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The navigation button used to return to recently visited Web pages in Internet Explorer, Microsoft Edge, and other internet browsers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1055132">Back</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1251284">ಹಿಂದೆ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22826_1055147_1956595"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A staging area that contains representations of selected objects and attributes in a connected data source.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1055147">connector space</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956595">ಕನೆಕ್ಟರ್ ಸ್ಥಳ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22828_1055149_1956755"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The data store that is used by ILM to contain the aggregated identity information from multiple connected data sources, providing a single global, integrated view of all combined objects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1055149">metaverse</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956755">ಮೆಟಾವರ್ಸ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2285_109836_1902974"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A join in which records from a table are combined with other records from the same table when there are matching values in the joined fields. A self-join can be an inner join or an outer join. In database diagrams, a self-join is called a reflexive relationship.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109836">self-join</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1902974">ಸ್ವಯಂ ಸೇರಿಸುವಿಕೆ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22865_1055946_1251285"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Information that describes the current location of a computer. The location is entered manually in Default Location, and can be used by programs to determine the location of a computer when a location sensor is unavailable.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1055946">default location</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1251285">ಪೂರ್ವನಿಯೋಜಿತ ಸ್ಥಳ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22865_1055946_1308213"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Information that describes the current location of a computer. The location is entered manually in Default Location, and can be used by programs to determine the location of a computer when a location sensor is unavailable.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1055946">default location</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1308213">ಪೂರ್ವನಿಯೋಜಿತ ಸ್ಥಾನ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22886_1056046_1984584"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software system that retrieves information from a source data store and synchronizes (pushes) to a target data store. Examples of synchronization engines are the ILM 2007 and FIM 2010 synchronization engines, and the service that synchronizes data rows in the SQL Server Express database with objects in the Microsoft Office Outlook data store.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056046">synchronization engine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1984584">ಸಿಂಕ್ರೊನೈಸೇಶನ್ ಎಂಜಿನ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22886_1056047_1984584"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software system that retrieves information from a source data store and synchronizes (pushes) to a target data store. Examples of synchronization engines are the ILM 2007 and FIM 2010 synchronization engines, and the service that synchronizes data rows in the SQL Server Express database with objects in the Microsoft Office Outlook data store.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056047">SyncEngine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1984584">ಸಿಂಕ್ರೊನೈಸೇಶನ್ ಎಂಜಿನ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22889_1056052_1956835"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To refuse to accept a file or message.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056052">reject</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956835">ನಿರಾಕರಿಸು</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2290_103825_473904"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Generally, any part of a computer system or network, such as a disk drive, printer, or memory, that can be allotted to a running program or a process.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="103825">resource</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="473904">ಸಂಪನ್ಮೂಲ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22904_1056071_1956571"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of components and services that enable users to access their Exchange mailboxes through the Outlook Web Access application.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056071">Client Access server</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956571">ಕ್ಲೈಂಟ್ ಪ್ರವೇಶ ಸರ್ವರ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2291_184207_1903104"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The hierarchical HTML tag structure of an opened HTML document that appears in a task pane window.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184207">tag tree</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1903104">ಟ್ಯಾಗ್ ಟ್ರೀ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22911_1056204_1251286"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A term that can be added to a search to filter the results by a specific property (for example, by author). Relevant search filters appear under the search box in any open folder.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056204">search filter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1251286">ಫಿಲ್ಟರ್ ಶೋಧನೆ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22919_1056243_1956514"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of Internet Protocol subnets, usually used to connect a group of computers that are physically close to each other.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056243">Active Directory site</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956514">Active Directory ಸೈಟ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22926_1056255_1956511"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of sign-in credentials (username and password) for an Active Directory account.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056255">Active Directory credentials</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956511">Active Directory ರುಜುವಾತುಗಳು</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termN