r</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2020858">ಬ್ಯಾಟರಿ ಮಟ್ಟ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24051_1097914_2028401"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To return to a stable condition after some error has occurred. A program recovers from an error by stabilizing itself and resuming execution of instructions without user intervention.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1097914">recover</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2028401">ಮರಳಿಪಡೆ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24057_1098418_1903402"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of statistics that indicates the degree to which a service meets performance, usage, and other demands for the service.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098418">service quality metrics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1903402">ಸೇವೆಯ ಗುಣಮಟ್ಟ ಮಾಪನಗಳು</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2407_73729_473710"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In programming, the order and sequence of input and output.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="73729">layout</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="473710">ಲೇಔಟ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24076_1098449_2688573"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The time during which a program is running. In most interactive programs, a session is the time during which the program accepts input and processes information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098449">session</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2688573">ಸೆಷನ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24102_1098534_1903403"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feed that provides users with information, notifications and updates based on people, documents, and tags they are following.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098534">activity feed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1903403">ಚಟುವಟಿಕೆಯ ಫೀಡ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="gramm