e inbound or outbound call and is a means of having concurrent calls on PBX.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1814023">calling channel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2074402">ಕರೆ ಚಾನಲ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33711_1814023_2074403"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A path enabling one inbound or outbound call and is a means of having concurrent calls on PBX.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1814023">calling channel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2074403">ಚಾನಲ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33711_1814024_2074402"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A path enabling one inbound or outbound call and is a means of having concurrent calls on PBX.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1814024">channel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2074402">ಕರೆ ಚಾನಲ್</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNo