ries (or categories) in a chart. Legend keys appear to the left of legend entries. Formatting a legend key also formats the data marker that's associated with it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="143969">legend keys</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250946">ಆಖ್ಯಾಯಿಕೆ ಕೀಲಿಗಳು</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="568_297005_474732"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program designed to amuse or scare a user, for example by imitating the actions of a virus, without actually harming the computer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="297005">joke program</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="474732">ಅಣಕು ಪ್ರೋಗ್ರಾಂ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5686_7496_473223"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device, such as a disk drive, printer, modem, or joystick, that is connected to a computer and is controlled by the computer's microprocessor.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7496">accessory</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="473223">ಉಪಕರಣ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote