Note></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956585">ಸಂಗ್ರಹ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6689_232848_474444"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A portion of a document in which you set certain page formatting options. You create a new section when you want to change such properties as line numbering, number of columns, or headers and footers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232848">section</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="474444">ವಿಭಾಗ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6700_232840_1250963"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Formatting applied to a heading. Microsoft Office Word has nine different built-in styles: Heading 1 through Heading 9.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232840">heading style</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1250963">ತಲೆಬರಹ ವಿನ್ಯಾಸ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6703_397177_1956735"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A mail-enabled Active Directory user object that has mailbox attributes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397177">mailbox user</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956735">ಮೇಲ್‌ಬಾಕ್ಸ್ ಬಳಕೆದಾರ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6707_307425_1956656"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A zone of non-communication between distinct departments of a business or organization to prevent conflicts of interest that might result in the inappropriate release of sensitive information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307425">ethical wall</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1956656">ನೀತಿತತ್ವದ ತಡೆ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6708_29444_1253177"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To align objects or text around a point located in the middle of a line, page, or other defined area; in effect, to position items an equal distance from each margin or border.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="29444">center</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="kn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1253177">ಮಧ್ಯೆ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="pa